Upstream-Name: Lunduke Civ
Upstream-Contact: Bryan Lunduke

Lunduke Civ is a turn-based empire-building game for one player against
computer rivals. Its rules follow the published tables of the 1991 DOS
game Sid Meier's Civilization (terrain yields, unit statistics, the
advance tree, combat and city growth), re-implemented from scratch. No
code, art, text, music or data files from that game are included.

All pixel art (terrain, rivers, cities, huts, the 28 unit counters and
the small icons) is original and is drawn by code in src/art. The user
interface follows the look of Lunduke City 2 (SDL3 for the window and
input; Cairo and Pango for drawing and text) and contains no art from
Lunduke City 2 or from Electronic Arts. The complete GNU GPL version 3
is in the file COPYING.

The Windows package adds DejaVu Sans and Sans Mono and the MSYS2 runtime
libraries it links; their licenses are copied into share/licenses by
packaging/windows/package.sh.

